Z||000000||BPacholka||10-16-2001||03:43 PM||||The heater fan in my 85 GT will only work in the lowest 3 positions. I flip it to high and it stops. Is anyone familar with how the fan works.||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-16-2001||06:57 PM||||Yeah - it blows air.  That's how it works!  You're welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>The only thing unique about the heater blowers' "high" speed is, it gets its power through a relay.  I don't remember where it's located, sorry, but someone on the forum will undoubtedly know.<P>After you find it, verify that the relay is getting juice (probably via a fusible link) to its "main supply" terminal - a big fat red or orange wire, I'm guessing.  Next,  verify that the relay's coil gets energized when you switch the blower to "high" (with the ignition on).  Finally, verify that the "output" terminal on the relay gets juice when you switch to "high."<P>Sorry I can't be any more descriptive than that.  I'm working from memory and lots of inexperience here... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> But that's the gist of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2001||07:58 PM||||That relay is located in the right front by the A/C duct work. There are 2 there, it's one of them.||||reg||1
